# JDK 9+ module system compatibility. Two independent consumers need these flags:
#   1. The Hazelcast client this process embeds to talk to the Zeta engine. Its own
#      serialization and networking internals reflectively touch these JDK APIs; nothing in
#      this codebase calls them directly, so there is no first-party call site in our source
#      to point to for these.
#   2. This project's own reflective Kerberos configuration reload helpers (KuduUtil,
#      PaimonSecurityContext) and the connector classloader injection helpers
#      (AbstractPluginDiscovery, ConfigValidationUtils, the Flink starter plugin loaders),
#      which are named per-flag below.
# Without these flags, the reflective access fails silently instead of raising a startup
# error, so the loss is easy to miss until the affected path is actually exercised.
# Required by Hazelcast client internals (see note 1 above).
--add-opens=java.base/java.lang=ALL-UNNAMED
# Required by URLClassLoader#addURL reflection: AbstractPluginDiscovery,
# ConfigValidationUtils, and the Flink starter plugin loaders inject connector jars this way.
--add-opens=java.base/java.net=ALL-UNNAMED
# Required by Hazelcast client internals (see note 1 above).
--add-opens=java.base/java.nio=ALL-UNNAMED
# Required by Hazelcast client internals (see note 1 above).
--add-opens=java.base/java.util=ALL-UNNAMED
# Required by Hazelcast client internals (see note 1 above).
--add-opens=java.base/sun.nio.ch=ALL-UNNAMED
# Required by the Kerberos configuration reload helpers KuduUtil and PaimonSecurityContext,
# which reflectively call io.debezium/sun.security.krb5.Config#refresh() equivalents to pick
# up a custom krb5.conf without a JVM restart.
--add-exports=java.security.jgss/sun.security.krb5=ALL-UNNAMED

# JVM Heap
-Xms256m
-Xmx512m

# JVM Dump
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=/tmp/seatunnel/dump/zeta-client